---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@lib/site';
import { withBase } from '@lib/url';

// Bump this when the terms materially change.
const lastUpdated = 'November 24, 2026';

const sections = [
  {
    id: 'agreement',
    heading: 'Agreement',
    body: [
      `These Terms of Use apply to the apps published by ${SITE.name}, operated by Marcus Wallberg in Sweden, and to this website. By downloading, buying or using one of our apps you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the app.`,
      'The terms of the store you got the app from, such as Google Play, also apply. If they conflict with these terms on purchases, payments or refunds, the store’s terms take precedence.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'licence',
    heading: 'Your Licence',
    body: [
      'We give you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the app on devices you own or control, for your own non-commercial use.',
      'The apps, including their design, text, graphics, animations, 3D models and code, belong to us or our licensors. You may not copy, sell, rent out, redistribute or reverse engineer them, except where the law explicitly allows it.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'purchases',
    heading: 'Purchases and Refunds',
    body: [
      'Paid apps and in-app purchases are sold through the app store, which handles payment, receipts and refunds under its own policies. Your statutory rights as a consumer are not affected.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'instructional-content',
    heading: 'Instructional Content and Safety',
    body: [
      'Some apps, such as Knots, show how to do practical things. This content is general information to help you learn. It is simplified: an animation or a 3D model cannot show everything about how a real rope, load or situation behaves.',
      'It is not professional training and not a substitute for instruction from a qualified person. Do not rely on a knot, hitch or lashing you have learned from an app where a failure could injure anyone or damage property, for example in climbing, rescue, work at height, lifting, towing, mooring or boating, unless you have been trained to tie, check and use it in that situation.',
      'Always check every knot before you load it, use rope and equipment suited to the job, back up anything that matters, and follow the instructions from the manufacturer of your equipment and any rules that apply to your activity. A correctly tied knot can still slip, jam or fail because of the rope, the load or how it is dressed and set.',
      'We work hard to make our content accurate, but we cannot guarantee that it is free from errors or complete. If you find something that looks wrong, please tell us so we can fix it.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'disclaimer',
    heading: 'Disclaimer',
    body: [
      'The apps are provided “as is” and “as available”. To the extent permitted by law, we make no warranties beyond those that cannot be excluded, and we do not promise that an app will always be available, uninterrupted or error-free.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'liability',
    heading: 'Limitation of Liability',
    body: [
      'To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any injury, loss or damage that results from how you use an app or the information in it, including from knots or techniques that were tied or used incorrectly, or that failed. You use the information at your own risk and are responsible for your own safety and the safety of others.',
      'To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, such as loss of data, income or opportunity.',
      'Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable law, such as liability for damage caused intentionally or through gross negligence, or your mandatory rights as a consumer.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'privacy',
    heading: 'Privacy',
    body: [
      'How our apps handle information is described in our Privacy Policy and in the privacy section of each app’s page.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'changes',
    heading: 'Changes',
    body: [
      'We may update these terms, for example when an app changes. The date at the top of this page shows when they were last updated. If you keep using an app after a change, the updated terms apply.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'law',
    heading: 'Governing Law',
    body: [
      'These terms are governed by Swedish law. If you are a consumer, you also keep the protection of mandatory rules in the country where you live.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'contact',
    heading: 'Contact',
    body: [
      `Questions about these terms, or something in an app that looks wrong? Email us at ${SITE.contactEmail}.`,
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`The terms for using ${SITE.author} apps, including how to use instructional content such as knots safely.`}
  path="/terms"
>
  <section class="container-page pt-16 pb-4">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
      <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl md:text-5xl">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-[var(--color-faint)]">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-page mt-10 pb-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-10">
      {sections.map((s) => (
        <div id={s.id}>
          <h2 class="text-2xl">{s.heading}</h2>
          {s.body.map((p) => (
            <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-muted)]">{p}</p>
          ))}
          {s.id === 'privacy' && (
            <p class="mt-3"><a class="underline" href={withBase('/privacy')}>Read the Privacy Policy</a></p>
          )}
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .kicker { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--color-peach-500); }
</style>
